Cell["\<\
Note that the area under this probability density function is 1.
We can determine the integral of the probability density which is called the \
probability distribution function (or the cumulative density function):\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.948978100577759*^9, 3.948978170003532*^9}, {
