Cell["\<\
Now we can see that the inter-sample intervals that were significantly \
different from the desired value of 0.02 s, only occurred a few times.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.948968153511917*^9, 3.94896815779991*^9}, {
  3.948968189362306*^9, 3.9489682205776567`*^9}, {3.9489685761092997`*^9, 
  3.948968660966778*^9}, {3.9489687614404163`*^9, 3.9489687717758617`*^9}, {
  3.980338271744821*^9, 
  3.980338273657155*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"31594575-386f-4497-9c5f-\
76b11a2293bf"],

Cell["\<\
It is clear that most of the inter-sample increments are at or close to the \
desired 0.02 s.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.948967358526219*^9, 
  3.948967412630145*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"afc3f1ad-1fe4-45a5-a660-\
f037680e9e2e"],

Cell["\<\
Probability density functions determined from data such as those above are \
termed non-parametric probability density functions to distinguish them from \
the parametric probability density functions such as Gaussian probability \
density functions which are specified by an equation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.948978248233458*^9, 3.9489784294820766`*^9}, {
  3.949416904049221*^9, 
  3.949416907183826*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"db4789a0-6c68-4af0-826b-\
ad5a7004d92d"]
}, Open  ]],

