Cell["\<\
As you can see this particular force sensor noise is not dependent upon force \
mean amplitude (at least not over this range).
Note that the assumption that measurement noise levels are independent on the \
amplitude of a signal is implicit when you use common least squares fitting \
of linear or nonlinear functions to data. If you have sensors where their \
noise levels change with amplitude then weighted least squares should be used.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9803594730099382`*^9, 3.9803595367785788`*^9}, {
  3.980359622129614*^9, 
  3.9803597779796762`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a6d4dc4e-29bd-45a4-8da2-\
0bc992180906"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
